  "solution": {
    "text": "Point of trisection nearer to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math>&nbsp;is <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>5,4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math><br />After rotation, the slope of the line is<br /><math><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">tan</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">tan</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mn>45</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">tan</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">tan</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mn>45</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">tan</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math> (where,&nbsp;<math><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">tan</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></math> is the slope of <math><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> )<br />Equation of the required line is <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>"
